course: dictionary
lesson: 5765
title: Lumpy: bumps and uneven
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Lumpy means full of lumps, not smooth. A lumpy surface has bumps on it, like a road full of potholes or a mattress with hard knobs under the cover.
explain: Use the clues around the word. «In the lumpy little valley the Mole trips and falls with a squeal» tells you two things: he trips, and the ground is uneven. So lumpy must describe ground with bumps, not flat ground.
explain: The same word can describe food and clothes too. «Auntie Siobhan hands Mum a lumpy orange jumper» means the jumper has bumps in its knitting, not a smooth finish. When you meet lumpy in a new place, ask: what is bumpy or uneven here?
fact: Lumpy means full of lumps, not smooth.
fact: The comparison forms are lumpy, lumpier, lumpiest.
fact: In cooking, porridge, gravy or custard goes lumpy when it has not been stirred well.
fact: «Hyperion is a lumpy moon like a sponge, full of deep craters.» A sponge has holes and bumps, so the picture helps you see the word.
fact: The opposite of lumpy is smooth.
exercise: «The stonefish looks exactly like a lumpy stone.» What does lumpy mean here? | Bright orange and spotted | Shiny and smooth like glass | Very quick and fast | *Full of lumps, not smooth
exercise: «Mum's custard was lumpy because nobody stirred it well.» What does lumpy suggest about the custard? | *It has small bits in it and is not smooth | It is sweet and very creamy | It is hot and steaming
exercise: Find and copy the one word from «Auntie Siobhan hands Mum a lumpy orange jumper» that describes the jumper. | Auntie | *lumpy | Dublin | Christmas
exercise: Hmm
test: «Hyperion is a lumpy moon like a sponge.» What kind of surface does a lumpy moon have? | One made of soft, warm sand | *One covered in bumps, dips and craters | One that gives off its own light | One that is smooth and round like a ball
test: Which word means the opposite of lumpy? | *smooth | bumpy | rough | knobbly
exam: Which sentence uses lumpy correctly? | *The old mattress was so lumpy that I could not sleep. | The bread was lumpy because it was flat and smooth. | The lake was lumpy and calm, like a sheet of glass. | My bedroom was lumpy and very quiet.
